==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|k|a}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*kaikki}}. Perhaps originally derived from a {{der|fi|bat|-}} language, cf. {{cog|lt|kiek||how many}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Pronoun===
{{fi-pron}}

# {{lb|fi|indefinite|in singular, without a main word}} [[everything]]
#: {{ux|fi|Tänään '''kaikki''' menee pieleen.|Today '''everything''' goes wrong.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Vihaan '''kaikkea.'''|I hate everything.}}
# {{lb|fi|indefinite|in plural, without a main word}} [[everyone]], [[everybody]]
#: {{ux|fi|'''Kaikki''' olivat täällä.|'''Everyone''' was here.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Vihaan '''kaikkia.'''|I hate everyone.}}
# {{lb|fi|in compounds}} [[all-]], [[omni-]]

===Determiner===
{{head|fi|determiner}}

# [[all]]
#: {{ux|fi|'''Kaikki''' sukkani löytyivät.|'''All''' my socks were found.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Yhtäkkiä '''kaikki''' vesi vyöryi huoneistoon.|Suddenly '''all''' the water ran into the apartment.}}

====Usage notes====
* The pronoun has also a nominative plural form ''kaiket'' which is used only in some phrases, e.g. ''kaiket [[päivä]]t'', "day after day" / "for days on end".

